    "show_share": true,
    "description": "\" Universities are vastly underutilised and potentially powerful vehicles for development in developing countries, particularly with respect to science and technology. If both universities and industry are encouraged to work actively together, universities will be able to assume new roles that could accelerate local and national development. \" - United Nations Millennium Project",
